On Sun, 30 Dec 2007, Henry J Cobb wrote:
> It's not like most rings can be used against you and the tight areas of
> Sokoban are some of the best places to deal with invisible monsters and
> such.

Actually, rings will never be used against you.  Monsters just don't wear
them.  (They never do anything with spellbooks, either.)

This actually makes the game harder in a few ways.  If monsters did wear
rings, it would be possible to nondestructively identify a ring even if
one already has its power as a permanent intrinsic.

If monsters wore rings, you could power up pets better.  For example, you
could:

 * charm a random monster that can wear armor, such as an elf.
 * drop a spare set of silver dragon scales, ring of fire resistance,
   and ring of poison resistance in front of it.
 * wait for it to wear all three
 * zap with polymorph

Then you could have a mount that is immune to beam attacks, fire traps,
blue jellies, and poison instakills.  You could also get stoning
resistance by going with yellow scales and an amulet of reflection -- but
you'd lose cold resistance unless you swap one of the rings.

